pective replacement, unmeasured in this phase.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"g3-r0007-balanced_target\",\n    \"status\": \"success\",\n    \"config\": {\n      \"embedding_dim\": 16,\n      \"hidden\": [\n        128,\n        64\n      ],\n      \"lr\": 0.001,\n      \"joint_mode\": \"observed\",\n      \"statistic_mode\": \"count\",\n      \"grouping_mode\": \"match\",\n      \"histogram_grouping\": \"match\",\n      \"histogram_pairing\": \"observed\",\n      \"target_query\": true,\n      \"separate_reads\": true,\n      \"group_balanced\": true,\n      \"learned_weights\": true\n    },\n    \"wall_seconds\": 820.33650380373,\n    \"cost\": null,\n    \"resources\": null,\n    \"note\": \"New candidate: equal occupied-match-group mass, inherited target-query separate-field retrieval. Utility must exceed both frozen source bests and the context hybrid incumbent; conditioning needs balanced_context and balanced_uniform controls. Local checks passed: Python compile/AST; identical Model AST across four modules; exact parameter allocation/order versus incumbent; nine inherited methods exact; numeric imports/no model I/O; 61 bounded diagnostic scalars. Independent scalar algebra checked 4681 exhaustive group/mask cases through length four, per-group mass, empty/padding/singleton, permutation, group-score-offset invariance, uniform reconstruction, extreme scores, and a constructive equal-mean/count/histogram collision distinguished by within-group weighting after norm matching. Scalar checks do not execute Torch. Failed attempts retained: initial runtime JSON parsing failed due truncated tool output and was replaced by in-process bounded summaries; first scalar harness failed tuple/list concatenation and passed after harness-only correction. No model execution, training, installation, test access or new empirical score. Host forward/backward and diagnostics remain pending. Source SHA256=ae07cfc238a702f3f917d2376779341d41249be731de3878c1e3b17e6b8545a4.\"\n  }\n]\n","exit