{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nr=json.loads(Path('runtime.json').read_text()); c=r['context']; protocol=r['required_study_protocol_ref']\nheld=['protocol '+protocol,'same source parent and scratch initialization of all inherited tensors','same appended head dimensions and initialization','same optimizer/loss, three epochs, batch size 4096, seed 42 and all first-six-day exposures','same frozen causal history limit 128, sample identities and validation scorer']\nstudy={\n'id':'g3-t002-fusion-incremental-event-readout',\n'protocol_ref':protocol,\n'evidence_refs':['g1-r0019-pooled_observed','g3-r0007-balanced_target','baseline-static','baseline-pooled','baseline-din'],\n'question':'Does the current balanced, separate-field target query add predictive utility to the complete pooled_observed model beyond a matched context query and active-capacity recombination of already pooled evidence?',\n'hypothesis':'Within-match-group category/context and brand/context event associations may carry incremental predictive information absent from pooled_observed summaries. Preserve the entire stronger source and add the current target readout via a zero-final-initialized residual head on inherited shared features plus the norm-matched d-vector. Utility must beat both frozen source bests, especially pooled_observed. A target-query advantage over the identical active-capacity context-query cell supports only incremental query utility in this fusion; superiority over active learned recombination of existing group means and uniform duplicated evidence is also required for an event-readout complementarity interpretation. Shared ancestry and the absence of locally supplied query-control outcomes make redundancy a serious alternative.',\n'nearest_work':[\n {'source_ref':'g1-r0019-pooled_observed; history_g1_r0019_pooled_observed.py SHA256 ca68bdb11d082057b8c7984e212e745331b2f33d4e8895dc4488efe13ad3ed02','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Inherit the complete predictor, including independent moments and identity/context/repeat/overlap/chronological-transition/global pooled-product observed-gap branches. Add an event retrieval residual without replacing its existing representation or widening its existing MLP.'},\n {'source_ref':'g3-r0007-balanced_target; history_g3_r0007_balanced_target.py SHA256 ae07cfc238a702f3f917d2376779341d41249be731de3878c1e3b17e6b8545a4','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Reuse its target versus history-context queries, separate category/brand reads, equal occupied-match-group mass, score architecture and norm matching, but fuse into the stronger complete source with an appended zero-final residual rather than the earlier smaller shared MLP. This is an operational combination, not a verified new architecture family.'},\n {'source_ref':'paper:din v4 content-sha256:5fee25f33f375e51b3ee9417d376ff9dbe2ea3628c932a7679ddfeb0feaaade2; primary text lines 250-277','verification':'read','difference':'DIN already supplies target-conditioned learned history pooling. Original DIN explicitly abandons softmax to retain intensity; this field-adapted inherited source uses separate softmaxes within match groups, equal group mass and norm matching. No exact DIN reproduction or priority claim.'},\n {'source_ref':'queryformer-paper-v1 arxiv:2609.16548v1 content-sha256:27673f600e2ebec40e365fc313871564fba4b3671c4ea65270bca8f8b1123473; section 5.2 lines 224-249','verification':'read','difference':'The participant table contrasts cross-attention query generation and attention removal in another task/split. Here no learned query generator, token bridge, multi-view expansion or claimed transfer: first establish whether the existing target read adds utility to the stronger pooled predictor with capacity and evidence controls.'},\n {'source_ref':'paper:dmr README commit 2c6e76804281954a3c969010a31712cd5054aca9 SHA256 656c9e5eec79c9843e907a555ede2bf0a66a0db3515916af3d655080057c5a75 lines 4-8','verification':'read','difference':'Author README confirms category, brand and behavior type without item IDs. No item embeddings, negatives, auxiliary labels or claimed DMR reproduction. Publisher full paper remains unavailable.'}],\n'inherited_components':['Unmodified source model classes and all original parameters, allocation order, frozen config switches and parent forward arithmetic from g1-r0019-pooled_observed','Five exact source helpers from g3-r0007-balanced_target: _encode, _score, _weights, _group_weights and _match_norm; separate read algebra adapted only to an explicit learned flag','Reuse the parent\\\\'s allocated but dormant 4226-parameter attention scorer, without reinitialization; all four cells allocate the same parameters','Frozen meta/batch interface; no model I/O, labels, optimizer changes, extra events, data preprocessing or new supervision'],\n'proposed_difference':'Append a bias-free 32-unit ReLU residual head to [inherited shared features, 16-dimensional readout]; zero its final weight only after every parent allocation. Keep parent output plus all six existing residual branches exactly. Cell target uses the current balanced target read; context replaces only target embeddings as query with global per-field history means while target-match memberships stay fixed; uniform zero-scales the same scores, duplicating the already available equal-occupied-group average of summed pools; pooled_duplicate actively scores and mixes the four existing summed group means with the same two target queries and shared scorer, then norm matches. The latter introduces no event-level evidence and retains active scorer capacity, but changes key/value granularity and between-group normalization together, so it is a replacement control, not a single-factor query contrast. All four share head shape, allocated parameter order and initial parent function. The candidate is mechanism-distinct from either frozen source through simultaneous prediction from the full pooled representation and event-level retrieval; novelty remains unverified.',\n'predictions':[\n 'Primary utility: target full-population validation ROC-AUC exceeds both 0.6302753100663608 (pooled_observed) and 0.6202303848951921 (balanced_target) under the frozen full protocol; Logloss must also be reported.',\n 'Conditioning: target minus context paired-seed AUC is positive; its failure leaves target-query utility unsupported even if the fusion improves.',\n 'Evidence/capacity: target outperforms active pooled_duplicate as well as uniform. Gains reproduced by these controls support capacity/reuse rather than incremental event evidence.',\n 'Label-free diagnostics reproduce the parent logits before the new residual, verify norms, mass, padding/empty/zero-length handling, and exhibit equal-parent synthetic histories with potentially different event readout. These checks are implementation evidence, not causal evidence of prediction benefit.',\n 'Report actual parameters, wall/train time, peak memory and full validation throughput/batch p50/p95 latency. Increased cost is expected; make no equal-compute efficiency claim from a matched-data-pass comparison.'\n],\n'falsifiers':[\n 'No gain over pooled_observed, or any apparent gain fails paired repetition: incremental utility remains unsupported for this implementation.',\n 'Context matches/exceeds target: no support for the specifically target-query mechanism. Match grouping remains target dependent in both cells.',\n 'Pooled_duplicate or uniform matches/exceeds target: extra active capacity or existing evidence suffices; do not claim new event-level complementarity.',\n 'Parent reproduction, padding, finite forward/backward or information-boundary checks fail: execution/implementation failure, not scientific refutation.',\n 'Host cost exceeds trial cap or repetition reserve: retain receipt and stop/reduce future scope without altering the fixed protocol or budget.'\n],\n'alternative_explanations':[\n 'Shared representations already encode the useful signal; the two source scores do not establish complementarity.',\n 'Extra head capacity or activating the formerly dormant scorer explains gains; context and active pooled_duplicate address this, while uniform matches allocation but has a zero-gradient scorer.',\n 'Scratch optimization, zero-final residual warm-up, validation checkpoint selection or seed noise changes performance without the hypothesized information gain.',\n 'Pooling-control between-group normalization and reduced key support can affect optimization; allocated and nominal active scorer counts do not prove equal effective capacity.',\n 'Norm matching controls magnitude but can remove useful intensity or amplify near-zero vectors; fallback rate and norm errors are measured.',\n 'Short/empty histories and rare behaviors have limited sample support; static snapshots have undocumented as-of dates; event histories are truncated at 128. No production causal validity or cross-task transfer is established.'\n],\n'contrasts':[\n {'parent_ref':'g1-r0019-pooled_observed','intervention':'fusion_target: preserve complete parent and add current balanced target event read plus residual head','control':'Both frozen sources g1-r0019-pooled_observed and g3-r0007-balanced_target; retain their exact source hashes/configs as utility controls, not capacity controls','held_fixed':held,'remaining_confounds':['New residual head and activated scorer add capacity versus either frozen source','Source-model comparison is not a mechanism contrast','Original stored sources are seed 42; repetition required'],'decision_if_supported':'Proceed to query and duplication contrasts; utility over both is necessary but insufficient.','decision_if_not_supported':'Record null/negative fusion; inspect diagnostics to separate invalid execution from redundancy; one failure does not refute all fusion designs.'},\n {'parent_ref':'g1-r0019-pooled_observed','intervention':'fusion_target: per-field current target embeddings query identical event keys/values','control':'fusion_context: history mean category/brand embeddings query identical event keys/values, partitions and residual head','held_fixed':held+['identical 4226-parameter active scorer, equal occupied-group mass and norm reference','all other model operations and parameter shapes'],'remaining_confounds':['History-context queries carry different distributions','Both retain target-dependent match membership','Repetition/cluster uncertainty may be unavailable in this phase'],'decision_if_supported':'Provisional query utility only if target also beats the stronger frozen source and duplicate controls; repeat paired seeds.','decision_if_not_supported':'Do not attribute a gain to target conditioning; context may suffice.'},\n {'parent_ref':'g1-r0019-pooled_observed','intervention':'fusion_target: learns within-match-group event weighting','control':'fusion_uniform: same scored graph multiplied by zero before softmax; equal-group uniform summary is a deterministic re-expression of existing summed group means','held_fixed':held+['identical allocated scorer, learned head and norm reference'],'remaining_confounds':['Uniform scorer receives zero gradient; this is allocated-capacity matching, not active-scorer matching','Target changes weights and directions within groups'],'decision_if_supported':'Rule out uniform duplication alone; require active pooled_duplicate and context contrasts for mechanism support.','decision_if_not_supported':'Existing pooled evidence plus the extra head suffices; target event weighting unsupported.'},\n {'parent_ref':'g1-r0019-pooled_observed','intervention':'fusion_target: event-level separate keys/values and equal occupied-group weight mass','control':'fusion_pooled_duplicate: same active scorer and residual head score only four existing summed group means, use learned mass between occupied groups, average the two field-query reads and norm match; inputs are pure functions of inherited shared features and group sizes','held_fixed':held+['identical allocated head and active scorer parameter counts','same existing shared features and targets; no new model tensor allocations by mode'],'remaining_confounds':['Changes key/value granularity and normalization together; a replacement control','Four pooled keys versus up to 128 event keys changes effective capacity, gradient geometry and measured cost'],'decision_if_supported':'Support incremental event-readout utility only together with query and source comparisons; no proof of unique mechanism or priority.','decision_if_not_supported':'A learned nonlinear reuse of inherited evidence explains the gain; retain pooled_duplicate if it is the better quality/cost option.'}\n],\n'cost_plan':{\n 'estimate_ref':'g1-r0019-pooled_observed measured wall 834.09s/train 714.53s/inference 27.52s; g3-r0007-balanced_target wall 820.34s/train 721.76s/inference 21.11s. Fused cost unmeasured, estimate 1000-1300s per full unit; hard cap 1760.9324324010606s. Starting remaining 23568.358632802963s includes preparation, failures and diagnostics.',\n 'all_variants_counted':True,\n 'attribution_reserve':'Initial four cells cost an estimated 4000-5200s, at most 7043.73s at the frozen per-trial cap; their controls are included, not free. Reserve 1000s for a consequential discriminating follow-up only if the final reserve and preparation ledger remain covered. Do not duplicate an unknown-state host call.',\n 'assessment_reserve':'Reserve 13500s for validation-only paired repetitions of target, closest query/duplicate controls and both frozen sources, targeting seeds 42,43,44; reuse matching committed seed-42 receipts only. A prospective five-model final suite would require ten additional seed-43/44 units after this round; use measured costs and current ledger before scheduling. At cap the whole five-model suite may not fit: omit optional follow-ups first, document omitted repetitions and keep single-seed claims preliminary. No test access or withheld assessment is requested.',\n 'stop_rule':'Do not run training in propose phase. Host owns execution and budget. Stop on actual remaining-budget/trial-cap limit, failed integrity checks, or when no useful admissible contrast fits after reserves. Never alter epochs/history/data/scorer or raise a cap. Freeze source/config/checkpoint comparison suite before any later assessment; current assessment scope is validation only.'\n}}\nassess=[]\nfor kid,decision,reason in [\n ('taac2026-academic-1-craft','considered','Card-only evidence of contextual residual transport; no local propagation-instability observation, reliability gates or distillation here. A generic zero-final residual for parent preservation is not an adoption of its contextual transport mechanism.'),\n ('taac2026-academic-2-unidac','rejected','Only organizer-level detail; no local old/recent compression bottleneck or new history budget. Do not map action types to source business domains or add a dual sequence path.'),\n ('taac2026-academic-3-unitokenformer','rejected','No measured tokenization bottleneck, detailed implementation or locally identified token-allocation need. No tokens or sequence decoder are introduced.'),\n ('taac2026-industry-1-queryformer','considered','Read archived v1 section 5.2 Table 4. Query-replacement concerns motivate careful attribution, but no query-generation/field-sequence bridge mechanism is adopted; the source task/split and removal contrasts cannot establish local incremental utility.'),\n ('taac2026-industry-2-unidot','considered','Card reports unresolved fusion tradeoff and capacity/optimization confounds. No per-layer FM interaction highway, bus fusion or source supervision is adopted; the present question concerns the already available readout.'),\n ('paper:din','used','Primary v4 section 4.3 read; inherited target-conditioned scoring is nearest prior work. Original unnormalized DIN differs from the current normalized, group-balanced field adaptation.'),\n ('paper:dmr','considered','Author README line 8 confirms available field identities without item IDs; publisher full text remains unavailable and no DMR mechanism is adopted.')]:\n assess.append({'knowledge_id':kid,'decision':decision,'rationale':reason,'transformed_mechanism': 'Inherited field-adapted local target relevance, combined with the full stronger pooled source through a zero-final residual; no novelty claim.' if kid=='paper:din' else 'None adopted from this source.', 'variant_names':['fusion_target','fusion_context','fusion_uniform','fusion_pooled_duplicate'] if kid=='paper:din' else [], 'nearest_work_difference':'Prospective combination and attribution in this frozen dataset; no cross-task transfer or priority established.', 'falsifier':'Target fails to beat pooled_observed, context, or active pooled duplication after paired repetition; diagnostics alone cannot validate predictive utility.'})\nproposal={'study':study,'parent_trial':'g1-r0019-pooled_observed','variants':[],'knowledge_assessments':assess,\n'observation_audit':{'phase':'propose','new_training_runs':0,'novelty':'unverified','prior_trajectories':[],'limitations':['Only the five allowed observation IDs are available. Earlier failures and abandoned branches are not supplied; lineage names alone are not outcomes. Do not invent or import other-arm results.','No local Torch runtime, raw data, checkpoints, validation labels or bootstrap interface. Host supplies training and scoring after proposal. Primary-source reads and AST/scalar checks do not reproduce empirical scores.','All retrieved industry cards are reviewed above; personal knowledge is disabled; append-only memory file is not authorized in this phase, so provenance and provisional observations are recorded here for host ingestion.']}}\nfor h in c['history']:\n proposal['observation_audit']['prior_trajectories'].append({k:h[k] for k in ['id','parent','status','source_sha256','parameters','train_seconds','wall_seconds','peak_gpu_bytes']})\n proposal['observation_audit']['prior_trajectories'][-1]['validation']={k:h['validation'][k] for k in ['auc','logloss','samples','inference_seconds','examples_per_second','batch_latency_ms_p50','batch_latency_ms_p95']}\nproposal['local_validation']={'status':'pending source and scalar checks; no Torch execution authorized or available'}\nPath('proposal.json').write_text(json.dumps(proposal,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nprint('Recorded prospective study and source evidence in proposal.json before implementation or host experimentation.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nr=json.loads(Path('runtime.json').read_text()); c=r['context']; protocol=r['required_study_protocol_ref']\nheld=['protocol '+protocol,'same source parent and scratch initialization of all inherited tensors','same appended head dimensions and initialization','same optimizer/loss, three epochs, batch size 4096, seed 42 and all first-six-day exposures','same frozen causal history limit 128, sample identities and validation scorer']\nstudy={\n'id':'g3-t002-fusion-incremental-event-readout',\n'protocol_ref':protocol,\n'evidence_refs':['g1-r0019-pooled_observed','g3-r0007-balanced_target','baseline-static','baseline-pooled','baseline-din'],\n'question':'Does the current balanced, separate-field target query add predictive utility to the complete pooled_observed model beyond a matched context query and active-capacity recombination of already pooled evidence?',\n'hypothesis':'Within-match-group category/context and brand/context event associations may carry incremental predictive information absent from pooled_observed summaries. Preserve the entire stronger source and add the current target readout via a zero-final-initialized residual head on inherited shared features plus the norm-matched d-vector. Utility must beat both frozen source bests, especially pooled_observed. A target-query advantage over the identical active-capacity context-query cell supports only incremental query utility in this fusion; superiority over active learned recombination of existing group means and uniform duplicated evidence is also required for an event-readout complementarity interpretation. Shared ancestry and the absence of locally supplied query-control outcomes make redundancy a serious alternative.',\n'nearest_work':[\n {'source_ref':'g1-r0019-pooled_observed; history_g1_r0019_pooled_observed.py SHA256 ca68bdb11d082057b8c7984e212e745331b2f33d4e8895dc4488efe13ad3ed02','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Inherit the complete predictor, including independent moments and identity/context/repeat/overlap/chronological-transition/global pooled-product observed-gap branches. Add an event retrieval residual without replacing its existing representation or widening its existing MLP.'},\n {'source_ref':'g3-r0007-balanced_target; history_g3_r0007_balanced_target.py SHA256 ae07cfc238a702f3f917d2376779341d41249be731de3878c1e3b17e6b8545a4','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Reuse its target versus history-context queries, separate category/brand reads, equal occupied-match-group mass, score architecture and norm matching, but fuse into the stronger complete source with an appended zero-final residual rather than the earlier smaller shared MLP. This is an operational combination, not a verified new architecture family.'},\n {'source_ref':'paper:din v4 content-sha256:5fee25f33f375e51b3ee9417d376ff9dbe2ea3628c932a7679ddfeb0feaaade2; primary text lines 250-277','verification':'read','difference':'DIN already supplies target-conditioned learned history pooling. Original DIN explicitly abandons softmax to retain intensity; this field-adapted inherited source uses separate softmaxes within match groups, equal group mass and norm matching. No exact DIN reproduction or priority claim.'},\n {'source_ref':'queryformer-paper-v1 arxiv:2609.16548v1 content-sha256:27673f600e2ebec40e365fc313871564fba4b3671c4ea65270bca8f8b1123473; section 5.2 lines 224-249','verification':'read','difference':'The participant table contrasts cross-attention query generation and attention removal in another task/split. Here no learned query generator, token bridge, multi-view expansion or claimed transfer: first establish whether the existing target read adds utility to the stronger pooled predictor with capacity and evidence controls.'},\n {'source_ref':'paper:dmr README commit 2c6e76804281954a3c969010a31712cd5054aca9 SHA256 656c9e5eec79c9843e907a555ede2bf0a66a0db3515916af3d655080057c5a75 lines 4-8','verification':'read','difference':'Author README confirms category, brand and behavior type without item IDs. No item embeddings, negatives, auxiliary labels or claimed DMR reproduction. Publisher full paper remains unavailable.'}],\n'inherited_components':['Unmodified source model classes and all original parameters, allocation order, frozen config switches and parent forward arithmetic from g1-r0019-pooled_observed','Five exact source helpers from g3-r0007-balanced_target: _encode, _score, _weights, _group_weights and _match_norm; separate read algebra adapted only to an explicit learned flag','Reuse the parent\\\\'s allocated but dormant 4226-parameter attention scorer, without reinitialization; all four cells allocate the same parameters','Frozen meta/batch interface; no model I/O, labels, optimizer changes, extra events, data preprocessing or new supervision'],\n'proposed_difference':'Append a bias-free 32-unit ReLU residual head to [inherited shared features, 16-dimensional readout]; zero its final weight only after every parent allocation. Keep parent output plus all six existing residual branches exactly. Cell target uses the current balanced target read; context replaces only target embeddings as query with global per-field history means while target-match memberships stay fixed; uniform zero-scales the same scores, duplicating the already available equal-occupied-group average of summed pools; pooled_duplicate actively scores and mixes the four existing summed group means with the same two target queries and shared scorer, then norm matches. The latter introduces no event-level evidence and retains active scorer capacity, but changes key/value granularity and between-group normalization together, so it is a replacement control, not a single-factor query contrast. All four share head shape, allocated parameter order and initial parent function. The candidate is mechanism-distinct from either frozen source through simultaneous prediction from the full pooled representation and event-level retrieval; novelty remains unverified.',\n'predictions':[\n 'Primary utility: target full-population validation ROC-AUC exceeds both 0.6302753100663608 (pooled_observed) and 0.6202303848951921 (balanced_target) under the frozen full protocol; Logloss must also be reported.',\n 'Conditioning: target minus context paired-seed AUC is positive; its failure leaves target-query utility unsupported even if the fusion improves.',\n 'Evidence/capacity: target outperforms active pooled_duplicate as well as uniform. Gains reproduced by these controls support capacity/reuse rather than incremental event evidence.',\n 'Label-free diagnostics reproduce the parent logits before the new residual, verify norms, mass, padding/empty/zero-length handling, and exhibit equal-parent synthetic histories with potentially different event readout. These checks are implementation evidence, not causal evidence of prediction benefit.',\n 'Report actual parameters, wall/train time, peak memory and full validation throughput/batch p50/p95 latency. Increased cost is expected; make no equal-compute efficiency claim from a matched-data-pass comparison.'\n],\n'falsifiers':[\n 'No gain over pooled_observed, or any apparent gain fails paired repetition: incremental utility remains unsupported for this implementation.',\n 'Context matches/exceeds target: no support for the specifically target-query mechanism. Match grouping remains target dependent in both cells.',\n 'Pooled_duplicate or uniform matches/exceeds target: extra active capacity or existing evidence suffices; do not claim new event-level complementarity.',\n 'Parent reproduction, padding, finite forward/backward or information-boundary checks fail: execution/implementation failure, not scientific refutation.',\n 'Host cost exceeds trial cap or repetition reserve: retain receipt and stop/reduce future scope without altering the fixed protocol or budget.'\n],\n'alternative_explanations':[\n 'Shared representations already encode the useful signal; the two source scores do not establish complementarity.',\n 'Extra head capacity or activating the formerly dormant scorer explains gains; context and active pooled_duplicate address this, while uniform matches allocation but has a zero-gradient scorer.',\n 'Scratch optimization, zero-final residual warm-up, validation checkpoint selection or seed noise changes performance without the hypothesized information gain.',\n 'Pooling-control between-group normalization and reduced key support can affect optimization; allocated and nominal active scorer counts do not prove equal effective capacity.',\n 'Norm matching controls magnitude but can remove useful intensity or amplify near-zero vectors; fallback rate and norm errors are measured.',\n 'Short/empty histories and rare behaviors have limited sample support; static snapshots have undocumented as-of dates; event histories are truncated at 128. No production causal validity or cross-task transfer is established.'\n],\n'contrasts':[\n {'parent_ref':'g1-r0019-pooled_observed','intervention':'fusion_target: preserve complete parent and add current balanced target event read plus residual head','control':'Both frozen sources g1-r0019-pooled_observed and g3-r0007-balanced_target; retain their exact source hashes/configs as utility controls, not capacity controls','held_fixed':held,'remaining_confounds':['New residual head and activated scorer add capacity versus either frozen source','Source-model comparison is not a mechanism contrast','Original stored sources are seed 42; repetition required'],'decision_if_supported':'Proceed to query and duplication contrasts; utility over both is necessary but insufficient.','decision_if_not_supported':'Record null/negative fusion; inspect diagnostics to separate invalid execution from redundancy; one failure does not refute all fusion designs.'},\n {'parent_ref':'g1-r0019-pooled_observed','intervention':'fusion_target: per-field current target embeddings query identical event keys/values','control':'fusion_context: history mean category/brand embeddings query identical event keys/values, partitions and residual head','held_fixed':held+['identical 4226-parameter active scorer, equal occupied-group mass and norm reference','all other model operations and parameter shapes'],'remaining_confounds':['History-context queries carry different distributions','Both retain target-dependent match membership','Repetition/cluster uncertainty may be unavailable in this phase'],'decision_if_supported':'Provisional query utility only if target also beats the stronger frozen source and duplicate controls; repeat paired seeds.','decision_if_not_supported':'Do not attribute a gain to target conditioning; context may suffice.'},\n {'parent_ref':'g1-r0019-pooled_observed','intervention':'fusion_target: learns within-match-group event weighting','control':'fusion_uniform: same scored graph multiplied by zero before softmax; equal-group uniform summary is a deterministic re-expression of existing summed group means','held_fixed':held+['identical allocated scorer, learned head and norm reference'],'remaining_confounds':['Uniform scorer receives zero gradient; this is allocated-capacity matching, not active-scorer matching','Target changes weights and directions within groups'],'decision_if_supported':'Rule out uniform duplication alone; require active pooled_duplicate and context contrasts for mechanism support.','decision_if_not_supported':'Existing pooled evidence plus the extra head suffices; target event weighting unsupported.'},\n {'parent_ref':'g1-r0019-pooled_observed','intervention':'fusion_target: event-level separate keys/values and equal occupied-group weight mass','control':'fusion_pooled_duplicate: same active scorer and residual head score only four existing summed group means, use learned mass between occupied groups, average the two field-query reads and norm match; inputs are pure functions of inherited shared features and group sizes','held_fixed':held+['identical allocated head and active scorer parameter counts','same existing shared features and targets; no new model tensor allocations by mode'],'remaining_confounds':['Changes key/value granularity and normalization together; a replacement control','Four pooled keys versus up to 128 event keys changes effective capacity, gradient geometry and measured cost'],'decision_if_supported':'Support incremental event-readout utility only together with query and source comparisons; no proof of unique mechanism or priority.','decision_if_not_supported':'A learned nonlinear reuse of inherited evidence explains the gain; retain pooled_duplicate if it is the better quality/cost option.'}\n],\n'cost_plan':{\n 'estimate_ref':'g1-r0019-pooled_observed measured wall 834.09s/train 714.53s/inference 27.52s; g3-r0007-balanced_target wall 820.34s/train 721.76s/inference 21.11s. Fused cost unmeasured, estimate 1000-1300s per full unit; hard cap 1760.9324324010606s. Starting remaining 23568.358632802963s includes preparation, failures and diagnostics.',\n 'all_variants_counted':True,\n 'attribution_reserve':'Initial four cells cost an estimated 4000-5200s, at most 7043.73s at the frozen per-trial cap; their controls are included, not free. Reserve 1000s for a consequential discriminating follow-up only if the final reserve and preparation ledger remain covered. Do not duplicate an unknown-state host call.',\n 'assessment_reserve':'Reserve 13500s for validation-only paired repetitions of target, closest query/duplicate controls and both frozen sources, targeting seeds 42,43,44; reuse matching committed seed-42 receipts only. A prospective five-model final suite would require ten additional seed-43/44 units after this round; use measured costs and current ledger before scheduling. At cap the whole five-model suite may not fit: omit optional follow-ups first, document omitted repetitions and keep single-seed claims preliminary. No test access or withheld assessment is requested.',\n 'stop_rule':'Do not run training in propose phase. Host owns execution and budget. Stop on actual remaining-budget/trial-cap limit, failed integrity checks, or when no useful admissible contrast fits after reserves. Never alter epochs/history/data/scorer or raise a cap. Freeze source/config/checkpoint comparison suite before any later assessment; current assessment scope is validation only.'\n}}\nassess=[]\nfor kid,decision,reason in [\n ('taac2026-academic-1-craft','considered','Card-only evidence of contextual residual transport; no local propagation-instability observation, reliability gates or distillation here. A generic zero-final residual for parent preservation is not an adoption of its contextual transport mechanism.'),\n ('taac2026-academic-2-unidac','rejected','Only organizer-level detail; no local old/recent compression bottleneck or new history budget. Do not map action types to source business domains or add a dual sequence path.'),\n ('taac2026-academic-3-unitokenformer','rejected','No measured tokenization bottleneck, detailed implementation or locally identified token-allocation need. No tokens or sequence decoder are introduced.'),\n ('taac2026-industry-1-queryformer','considered','Read archived v1 section 5.2 Table 4. Query-replacement concerns motivate careful attribution, but no query-generation/field-sequence bridge mechanism is adopted; the source task/split and removal contrasts cannot establish local incremental utility.'),\n ('taac2026-industry-2-unidot','considered','Card reports unresolved fusion tradeoff and capacity/optimization confounds. No per-layer FM interaction highway, bus fusion or source supervision is adopted; the present question concerns the already available readout.'),\n ('paper:din','used','Primary v4 section 4.3 read; inherited target-conditioned scoring is nearest prior work. Original unnormalized DIN differs from the current normalized, group-balanced field adaptation.'),\n ('paper:dmr','considered','Author README line 8 confirms available field identities without item IDs; publisher full text remains unavailable and no DMR mechanism is adopted.')]:\n assess.append({'knowledge_id':kid,'decision':decision,'rationale':reason,'transformed_mechanism': 'Inherited field-adapted local target relevance, combined with the full stronger pooled source through a zero-final residual; no novelty claim.' if kid=='paper:din' else 'None adopted from this source.', 'variant_names':['fusion_target','fusion_context','fusion_uniform','fusion_pooled_duplicate'] if kid=='paper:din' else [], 'nearest_work_difference':'Prospective combination and attribution in this frozen dataset; no cross-task transfer or priority established.', 'falsifier':'Target fails to beat pooled_observed, context, or active pooled duplication after paired repetition; diagnostics alone cannot validate predictive utility.'})\nproposal={'study':study,'parent_trial':'g1-r0019-pooled_observed','variants':[],'knowledge_assessments':assess,\n'observation_audit':{'phase':'propose','new_training_runs':0,'novelty':'unverified','prior_trajectories':[],'limitations':['Only the five allowed observation IDs are available. Earlier failures and abandoned branches are not supplied; lineage names alone are not outcomes. Do not invent or import other-arm results.','No local Torch runtime, raw data, checkpoints, validation labels or bootstrap interface. Host supplies training and scoring after proposal. Primary-source reads and AST/scalar checks do not reproduce empirical scores.','All retrieved industry cards are reviewed above; personal knowledge is disabled; append-only memory file is not authorized in this phase, so provenance and provisional observations are recorded here for host ingestion.']}}\nfor h in c['history']:\n proposal['observation_audit']['prior_trajectories'].append({k:h[k] for k in ['id','parent','status','source_sha256','parameters','train_seconds','wall_seconds','peak_gpu_bytes']})\n proposal['observation_audit']['prior_trajectories'][-1]['validation']={k:h['validation'][k] for k in ['auc','logloss','samples','inference_seconds','examples_per_second','batch_latency_ms_p50','batch_latency_ms_p95']}\nproposal['local_validation']={'status':'pending source and scalar checks; no Torch execution authorized or available'}\nPath('proposal.json').write_text(json.dumps(proposal,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nprint('Recorded prospective study and source evidence in proposal.json before implementation or host experimentation.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"/bin/bash: warning: setlocale: LC_ALL: cannot change locale (C.UTF-8)\n/bin/bash: warning: setlocale: LC_ALL: cannot change locale (C.UTF-8)\nRecorded prospective study and source evidence in proposal.json before implementation or host experimentation.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport ast,json,hashlib\nparent=Path('history_g1_r0019_pooled_observed.py').read_text()\nassert hashlib.sha256(parent.encode()).hexdigest()=='ca68bdb11d082057b8c7984e212e745331b2f33d4e8895dc4488efe13ad3ed02'\nsource=Path('history_g3_r0007_balanced_target.py').read_text()\nassert hashlib.sha256(source.encode()).hexdigest()=='ae07cfc238a702f3f917d2376779341d41249be731de3878c1e3b17e6b8545a4'\ntree=ast.parse(source); cls=next(n for n in tree.body if isinstance(n,ast.ClassDef) and n.name=='Model')\nmethods={n.name:'\\\\n'.join(source.splitlines()[n.lineno-1:n.end_lineno]) for n in cls.body if isinstance(n,ast.FunctionDef)}\nhelpers='\\\\n\\\\n'.join(methods[n] for n in ['_encode','_score','_weights','_group_weights','_match_norm'])\n# Preserve decorators, which lie before FunctionDef.lineno.\nhelpers=helpers.replace('    def _weights(', '    @staticmethod\\\\n    def _weights(').replace('    def _group_weights(', '    @staticmethod\\\\n    def _group_weights(').replace('    def _match_norm(', '    @staticmethod\\\\n    def _match_norm(')\nread=methods['_read'].replace('def _read(', 'def _fusion_read(').replace('query, membership):','query, membership, learned=True):').replace('scale = float(self.learned_weights)', 'scale = float(learned)')\nnew_class='''\n\nclass Model(_PooledObservedModel):\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Complete pooled predictor plus a controlled history-readout residual.\n\n    Modes share all allocations and start with the exact parent's function.\n    Context replaces only query construction. Uniform duplicates inherited\n    evidence with an inactive scorer; pooled_duplicate is an active scorer\n    control using only pre-existing group means, sizes and target embeddings.\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    def __init__(self, meta, config=None):\n        super().__init__(meta, config)\n        self.fusion_mode = self.config['fusion_mode']\n        if self.fusion_mode not in ('target', 'context', 'uniform', 'pooled_duplicate'):\n            raise ValueError('Unknown fusion_mode')\n        self.group_balanced = True\n        self.static_width = len(meta['fields']) * self.config['embedding_dim']\n        dim = self.config['embedding_dim']\n        # Parent attention is allocated in every inherited model but dormant.\n        # Reuse it with its original initialization: do not allocate a second\n        # scorer or consume any random draw before the complete parent exists.\n        # Existing first-layer shape fixes the exact inherited feature width.\n        width = self.output[0].in_features + dim\n        self.fusion_head = nn.Sequential(\n            nn.Linear(width, self.config['fusion_hidden'], bias=False), nn.ReLU(),\n            nn.Linear(self.config['fusion_hidden'], 1, bias=False)\n        )\n        nn.init.zeros_(self.fusion_head[-1].weight)\n\n    def _fusion_base(self, batch):\n        # Exact _ParentModel._parent_forward arithmetic, exposing its shared\n        # features without a cache or a repeated embedding pass. Then append\n        # the exact chronological transition and pooled observed gap residuals.\n        features, _, _, _, _, semantic, _ = self._shared_features(batch)\n        tables = self._identity_tables(batch, semantic)\n        context = self._context_tables(batch, tables)\n        parent = self.output(features).squeeze(-1)\n        identity = self.identity_head(self._identity_features(tables)).squeeze(-1)\n        extra = self.context_head(self._context_features(context)).squeeze(-1)\n        repeat_tables = self._conditional_tables(batch, tables, context)\n        repeat = self.repeat_head(self._repeat_features(repeat_tables)).squeeze(-1)\n        overlap_tables = self._overlap_tables(batch, tables, context)\n        overlap = self.overlap_head(self._overlap_features(overlap_tables)).squeeze(-1)\n        parent = parent + identity + extra + repeat + overlap\n        transition = self._transition_tables(batch)\n        parent = parent + self.transition_head(self._transition_features(transition)).squeeze(-1)\n        gap = self._gap_features(self._gap_tables(batch))\n        parent = parent + self.gap_head(gap).squeeze(-1)\n        return parent, features\n'''\nrest='''\n\n    def _pooled_retrieval(self, features, sizes):\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Pure recombination of inherited shared features and group counts.\n\n        The four summed group means are already inputs to the parent MLP.\n        Their sizes are n-c-b+j, c-j, b-j, j from its match-count statistics.\n        These are sufficient to reconstruct the global reference mean, too.\n        Both target queries are slices of the existing static feature block.\n        This scorer is active; only its keys/values have been compressed.\n        Softmax is across occupied groups, rather than fixed group masses.\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\n        dim = self.config['embedding_dim']\n        start = self.static_width\n        pools = features[:, start:start + 4 * dim].reshape(features.shape[0], 4, dim)\n        target_c = features[:, self.category * dim:(self.category + 1) * dim]\n        target_b = features[:, self.brand * dim:(self.brand + 1) * dim]\n        mask = sizes > 0\n        membership = mask[:, None, :].to(pools.dtype)\n        wc = self._group_weights(self._score(target_c, pools), membership)\n        wb = self._group_weights(self._score(target_b, pools), membership)\n        raw = (0.5 * (wc + wb).unsqueeze(-1) * pools).sum(1)\n        pooled = (pools * sizes.unsqueeze(-1)).sum(1) / sizes.sum(-1, keepdim=True).clamp_min(1)\n        return {'summary': self._match_norm(raw, pooled), 'raw': raw,\n                'pooled': pooled, 'wc': wc, 'wb': wb, 'mask': mask}\n\n    def _retrieval(self, batch, features=None, mode=None):\n        mode = self.fusion_mode if mode is None else mode\n        if mode == 'pooled_duplicate':\n            if features is None:\n                features = self._shared_features(batch)[0]\n            sizes = self._membership(batch)[2]\n            return self._pooled_retrieval(features, sizes)\n        _, category, brand, common, mask, pooled, target, context = self._encode(batch)\n        semantic = self._membership(batch)[1]\n        query = context if mode == 'context' else target\n        raw, wc, wb, _, _, _, _ = self._fusion_read(\n            category, brand, common, mask, query, semantic, learned=(mode \"'!= '\"'uniform'))\n        return {'summary': self._match_norm(raw, pooled), 'raw': raw,\n                'pooled': pooled, 'wc': wc, 'wb': wb, 'mask': mask}\n\n    def forward(self, batch):\n        parent, features = self._fusion_base(batch)\n        readout = self._retrieval(batch, features)['summary']\n        residual = self.fusion_head(torch.cat([features, readout], -1)).squeeze(-1)\n        return parent + residual\n\n    def _fusion_witness(self, batch):\n        # Both histories have unique category and brand identities and share\n        # every marginal mean, coarse action/age table and recurrence count.\n        # Only category versus fine log2-age association changes. All timestamps\n        # are distinct, under one hour, with identical gaps. Target 5 is absent.\n        device = batch['static'].device\n        witness = {\n            'static': batch['static'][:1].expand(2, -1).clone(),\n            'history_category': torch.tensor([[1, 2, 3, 4], [4, 3, 2, 1]], dtype=torch.long, device=device),\n            'history_brand': torch.tensor([[1, 2, 3, 4], [1, 2, 3, 4]], dtype=torch.long, device=device),\n            'history_type': torch.ones((2, 4), dtype=torch.long, device=device),\n            'history_age_seconds': torch.tensor([[100, 200, 300, 400]] * 2,\n                                               dtype=batch['history_age_seconds'].dtype, device=device),\n            'history_mask': torch.ones((2, 4), dtype=torch.bool, device=device),\n        }\n        witness['static'][:, self.category] = 5\n        witness['static'][:, self.brand] = 5\n        return witness\n\n    def diagnostics(self, batch):\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Bounded label-free checks; predictive attribution needs host scores.\n\n        Run only on the host's fixed first-512 validation diagnostic batch.\n        Witnesses probe information and checkpoint sensitivity, never utility.\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\n        def maximum(x):\n            return x.abs().max() if x.numel() else x.new_zeros(())\n\n        parent, features = self._fusion_base(batch)\n        original_parent = _PooledObservedModel.forward(self, batch)\n        reads = {mode: self._retrieval(batch, features, mode)\n                 for mode in ('target', 'context', 'uniform', 'pooled_duplicate')}\n        read = reads[self.fusion_mode]\n        summary = read['summary']\n        residual = self.fusion_head(torch.cat([features, summary], -1)).squeeze(-1)\n        mask = batch['history_mask']\n        n = mask.float().sum(-1)\n        _, semantic, sizes = self._membership(batch)\n        occupied = sizes > 0\n        prior = occupied.float() / occupied.sum(-1, keepdim=True).clamp_min(1)\n        mass = torch.stack([(semantic * reads['target'][k][:, None, :]).sum(-1)\n                            for k in ('wc', 'wb')])\n        dim = self.config['embedding_dim']\n        pools = features[:, self.static_width:self.static_width + 4 * dim].reshape(features.shape[0], 4, dim)\n        uniform_raw = (pools * prior.unsqueeze(-1)).sum(1)\n        uniform_summary = self._match_norm(uniform_raw, reads['uniform']['pooled'])\n        active = read['mask'].any(-1).float()\n        result = {\n            'allocated_parameters': float(sum(p.numel() for p in self.parameters())),\n            'appended_head_parameters': float(sum(p.numel() for p in self.fusion_head.parameters())),\n            'scorer_parameters': float(sum(p.numel() for p in self.attention.parameters())),\n            'scorer_active_by_design': float(self.fusion_mode 